outcome:   a run that did not resolve every goal is INCOMPLETE, and
           its timings mean nothing: a sweep that aborts early looks
           fast. Compare only complete runs.
sat>=90%:  samples at or above 90% of every core busy
loop>=90%: samples where the event-loop thread alone held ~a full
           core -- with a low process figure beside it, that is the
           starvation signature: workers idle, waiting on the loop
dev util:  fraction of wall time the device had a request in flight
           (io_ticks/elapsed). 100% is saturation; MB/s is not.
dev q:     mean requests in flight (weighted io ms / elapsed). Above
           1 means requests were queueing behind each other.
thr D:     mean of OUR threads in uninterruptible sleep, over the
           N samples that carry a census (shown as mean/N). A busy
           device with thr D at 0 is somebody else's I/O, not ours.
-:         not measured on this host, which is not the same as zero
